  "title": "tshark: Always dynamically allocate dfilter",
  "description": "In one case `dfilter` was allocated with `g_malloc` (in `get_args_as_string`)\nwhile in the other was pointing to an `optarg`. Properly free `dfilter`\nbefore exit.\n\n```\n$ ctest -R suite_dissection -V\n\n21: test_communityid_filter (suite_dissection.case_communityid) ... FAIL\n\n21: Direct leak of 46 byte(s) in 1 object(s) allocated from:\n21:     #0 0x564b48dd7ebf in malloc (/home/vasko/sources/wireshark/build_clang/run/tshark+0x1f1ebf)\n21:     #1 0x7fb0cd2fdbb8 in g_malloc (/lib64/libglib-2.0.so.0+0x5bbb8)\n21:     #2 0x564b48e100ef in main /home/vasko/sources/wireshark/tshark.c:1586:17\n21:     #3 0x7fb0cd0b51e1 in __libc_start_main (/lib64/libc.so.6+0x281e1)\n```",
